From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 20:34:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 082/190] segacd: the retry fill gets double patience

Reads now land most of the time -- three errors a round, mispairs
corrected -- but a FAT walk needs eight consecutive clean blocks, and
the survivors are pure timeouts: a few genuinely hard spots on the
burn that a 1992 lens needs more tries at than the leash allows.
Sega's sample code answers exactly this with thirty reissues. The
second fill now runs at twice the leash; the first stays short, so a
healthy read never feels it.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 9ad8236..73a2a2c 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -2165,13 +2165,28 @@ static BOOL cd_read_block(ULONG block, UBYTE *buf)
          * meaningless -- the first try would spend the lot and the
          * second would find nothing left and return without asking the
          * drive anything, which is not a retry. */
-        for (go = 0; go < 2; go++) {
-            cd_epoch = cdd_ticks;
-            cd_budget = CD_SPIN_BACKSTOP;
-            if (cd_fill(lba))
-                break;
-            if (go)
-                return FALSE;
+        {
+            UWORD leash = cd_leash;
+
+            for (go = 0; go < 2; go++) {
+                cd_epoch = cdd_ticks;
+                cd_budget = CD_SPIN_BACKSTOP;
+                /* The second fill is the one that faces a genuinely
+                 * hard sector -- the first already spent a full leash
+                 * on it -- and Sega's sample code answers that case
+                 * with patience, thirty reissues, not cleverness.
+                 * Doubling the retry's leash is the same posture at
+                 * half the ceiling; the first fill stays short so a
+                 * healthy read never feels any of this. */
+                cd_leash = go ? (UWORD)(leash * 2) : leash;
+                if (cd_fill(lba))
+                    break;
+                if (go) {
+                    cd_leash = leash;
+                    return FALSE;
+                }
+            }
+            cd_leash = leash;
         }
     }
     memcpy(buf, cd_cache[lba - cd_cache_base] + off, SECTOR_SIZE);
